From 96f33074ade81f65f6b2871247a099b011c42334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 09:12:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0146 -- wave-51 _blit_indexed blit-decomp
 instrumentation

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-51-ASM-BLIT-DESIGN.md sec. 5 + the
0146 instrumentation contract. This is the INSTRUMENTATION ride-along
for the wave-51 asm opaque-span lever (patch 0145) -- NOT a second
lever. Per [[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]
it rides along on its OWN env gate, fully decoupled from 0145's
internals: instrumentation is measurement, not a mechanism.

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: the 0145 asm lever's honest fps ceiling (+2.0-2.5
fps) is conditional on two unknowns the analytical pass could not
resolve from existing logs -- the opaque-pixel fraction of the BG
tilemap and the per-tile opaque-run contiguity. If runs are fragmented
the precompute-table overhead eats the gain. 0146 measures both in the
SAME iter that A/Bs the lever, so a weak wave-51 delta is explained
rather than mysterious.

ENV GATE: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP (strict "1" opt-in; default
OFF). Cached-at-boot static-const-bool (_blit_decomp_enabled(),
modelled on _strict_truthy_env) -- never a per-call getenv (the
wave-38 STALL_REPORT per-call getenv cost -14 fps; that lesson is
encoded here). When the bool is false every counter/timer below is
untouched: the two clean PLAY cells (BLIT_DECOMP=0) pay exactly zero.

WHAT IT MEASURES (accumulated in `_blit_indexed`, emitted per 100-flip
block to the engine <TAG>.LOG via LOG_INFO, aligned to the existing
flip-stat / flip-body-stat 100-flip cadence -- _maybe_flush_phase_
timing_audit; own accumulators, reset at that boundary):

1. PHASE SPLIT -- 3 SDL_GetTicksNS reads (entry / clip-done / blit-
   branch-end). bi_dispatch = entry -> clip math done; bi_innerloop =
   the asm-or-colorkey blit branch. Per-flip accumulation -> one
   sample/flip pushed by flip() -> _compute_flip_phase_stats (the
   wave-20 STAT machinery) -> `[blit-decomp-stat n=N phase=bi_dispatch
   |bi_innerloop min/med/mean/p95/max ms]`. bi_innerloop is the
   essential A/B: PLAY1 (asm on) times the span path, PLAY2 (asm
   off) times the colorkey loop -- the delta IS the lever.

2. PIXEL CENSUS -- per-block integer counters: px_total / px_opaque
   (px != colorkey) / px_skipped (== colorkey). Emits
   `[blit-decomp-census n=N caller=<bg|other> px_total=.. px_opaque=..
   px_skipped=.. opaque_pct_x10=..]`.

3. RUN CENSUS -- run_count (contiguous opaque runs) + a {1-3,4-8,
   9-15,>=16} run-length histogram, counted by a per-row rising-edge
   state machine inside the instrumented colorkey loop. Emits
   `[blit-decomp-runs n=N caller=<bg|other> run_count=.. hist_1_3=..
   hist_4_8=.. hist_9_15=.. hist_16=..]`. This is the direct sizing
   input for the 0145 asm ceiling.

4. CALLER SPLIT -- counts 2+3 are split by the existing wave-25
   g_mds_tfg_loop_active flag (cc=0 BG/FG tilemap loop, cc=1
   sprite/HUD) so BG and sprite opaque fractions are separable.

LEVER-INDEPENDENCE (contract Q2): the px/run census counting code
lives INSIDE the legacy per-pixel colorkey loop in `_blit_indexed`,
gated on BLIT_DECOMP -- it is NOT derived from 0145's span table.
PLAY2 (ASM_BLIT=0, lever off) runs the colorkey loop and yields the
full baseline census -- that is THE sizing measurement. In PLAY1
(ASM_BLIT=1) the span path is taken and the census reads ~0; that
asymmetry is expected and documented in the emit comment. To keep the
BLIT_DECOMP=OFF path byte-identical, the colorkey branch is split
`else if (has_colorkey && _bd_on) { instrumented loop } else if
(has_colorkey) { plain loop }` -- the plain loop is the 0145 loop
unchanged.

COST: 3 SDL_GetTicksNS reads/call (~90 cyc) + ~6 int ops/row in the
instrumented colorkey loop. At ~150-336 calls/flip ~ 0.1-0.25 ms/flip
-- ACCEPTABLE, and only the two INSTR PLAY cells (PLAY1/PLAY2) carry
it; PLAY3/PLAY4 run BLIT_DECOMP=0 and pay zero.

NO COLLISION WITH WAVE-25: the patch-0111 wave-25 brackets (gated on
g_mds_tfg_loop_active, bracket the WHOLE body) are untouched -- the
0146 timers use a separate gate + separate accumulators and nest
strictly inside. The 3rd SDL_GetTicksNS read sits exactly at the
clip-done branch point.

FILES: src/graphics/Renderer.cpp only (~110 LOC; file-scope blit-decomp
state + _blit_decomp_enabled gate + _bd_record_run helper;
`_blit_indexed` 3-read phase split + instrumented colorkey loop;
flip() per-flip sample fill; _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit emit +
reset; initVideo banner).

PLAY MATRIX (which cells carry it): PLAY1 = ASM_BLIT=1 + BLIT_DECOMP=1;
PLAY2 = ASM_BLIT=0 + BLIT_DECOMP=1; PLAY3/PLAY4 = BLIT_DECOMP=0.

Banner regex for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS:
"Renderer::initVideo: blit-decomp .* instrumentation (ENABLED|DISABLED)"
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 191 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 191 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index 4d85d95..bac36b4 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -1579,6 +1579,50 @@ Uint64 _flip_body_samples_audit_flushes[_flip_phase_block_size]    = {};
 Uint64 _flip_body_samples_residual[_flip_phase_block_size]         = {};
 int    _flip_body_sample_idx = 0;
 
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0146, Phase 11 wave-51): `_blit_indexed` sub-decomp
+// instrumentation storage. Rides along with the 0145 asm opaque-span
+// lever (own env gate SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP per single-lever
+// discipline -- measurement, not a mechanism). Two phase-timer sample
+// arrays carry one sample per flip (the per-flip accumulated ns);
+// flip() fills them at the 100-flip emit boundary, same cadence as
+// flip-stat / flip-body-stat. The px/run census counters are per-100-
+// flip-block, split [0]=bg (wave-25 g_mds_tfg_loop_active set) vs
+// [1]=other (sprite/HUD). Everything here is untouched when the
+// BLIT_DECOMP gate is OFF (the two clean PLAY cells pay zero).
+Uint64 _bd_dispatch_samples[_flip_phase_block_size]  = {};
+Uint64 _bd_innerloop_samples[_flip_phase_block_size] = {};
+int    _bd_sample_idx = 0;
+Uint64 _bd_dispatch_ns_this_flip  = 0;
+Uint64 _bd_innerloop_ns_this_flip = 0;
+Uint64 _bd_px_total[2]    = {};
+Uint64 _bd_px_opaque[2]   = {};
+Uint64 _bd_px_skipped[2]  = {};
+Uint64 _bd_run_count[2]   = {};
+Uint64 _bd_run_hist[2][4] = {};   // run-length buckets {1-3, 4-8, 9-15, >=16}
+
+// Cached-at-boot gate for the blit-decomp instrumentation. Strict "1"
+// opt-in; evaluated once. Modelled on _strict_truthy_env per the
+// project diagnostic-hint convention (wave-25 / FLIP_INSTR siblings).
+inline bool _blit_decomp_enabled()
+{
+  static const bool v = _strict_truthy_env("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP");
+  return v;
+}
+
+// Bucket one contiguous opaque-run length into the {1-3,4-8,9-15,>=16}
+// histogram for caller class cc. Called only from the BLIT_DECOMP-gated
+// instrumented colorkey loop in `_blit_indexed` -- zero-cost when OFF.
+inline void _bd_record_run(int cc, int run_len)
+{
+  ++_bd_run_count[cc];
+  int b;
+  if (run_len <= 3)       b = 0;
+  else if (run_len <= 8)  b = 1;
+  else if (run_len <= 15) b = 2;
+  else                    b = 3;
+  ++_bd_run_hist[cc][b];
+}
+
 // DOS-PORT (patch 0087, Phase 9 wave 20 Lever A): summarize a sample
 // array. n must be <= _flip_phase_block_size; copy is on-stack so total
 // stack pressure is ~4 KB across the 5 phases x invocation site (one
@@ -2032,6 +2076,61 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
   NXE::Diag::g_drawtile_fast_bg_fallback_count_block = 0;
   NXE::Diag::g_drawtile_fast_bg_calls_count_block    = 0;
 
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0146, Phase 11 wave-51): emit `_blit_indexed`
+  // sub-decomp lines -- 2 STAT lines (bi_dispatch / bi_innerloop) +
+  // per-caller-class census + run-census. bi_innerloop times the
+  // asm-or-colorkey blit branch: PLAY1 vs PLAY2 bi_innerloop IS the
+  // 0145 lever A/B. The px/run census reads non-zero only in PLAY2
+  // (ASM_BLIT=0 -- legacy colorkey loop runs); in PLAY1 the span path
+  // is taken and the census reads ~0 (expected -- PLAY2 is the
+  // baseline sizing cell, see WAVE-51-ASM-BLIT-DESIGN sec. 5).
+  if (_blit_decomp_enabled() && _bd_sample_idx > 0)
+  {
+    const int n_bd = _bd_sample_idx;
+    _FlipPhaseStats st_bd_disp, st_bd_inner;
+    _compute_flip_phase_stats(_bd_dispatch_samples,  n_bd, st_bd_disp);
+    _compute_flip_phase_stats(_bd_innerloop_samples, n_bd, st_bd_inner);
+    LOG_INFO("[blit-decomp-stat n={} phase=bi_dispatch  min={:.2f} med={:.2f} mean={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} ms]",
+             n_bd, st_bd_disp.min_ms, st_bd_disp.med_ms, st_bd_disp.mean_ms, st_bd_disp.p95_ms, st_bd_disp.max_ms);
+    LOG_INFO("[blit-decomp-stat n={} phase=bi_innerloop min={:.2f} med={:.2f} mean={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} ms]",
+             n_bd, st_bd_inner.min_ms, st_bd_inner.med_ms, st_bd_inner.mean_ms, st_bd_inner.p95_ms, st_bd_inner.max_ms);
+    for (int cc = 0; cc < 2; ++cc)
+    {
+      const char *cname = (cc == 0) ? "bg" : "other";
+      const Uint64 tot = _bd_px_total[cc];
+      const long long opct_x10 =
+          (tot > 0) ? (long long)((_bd_px_opaque[cc] * 1000ull) / tot) : 0;
+      LOG_INFO("[blit-decomp-census n={} caller={} px_total={} px_opaque={} px_skipped={} opaque_pct_x10={}]",
+               n_bd, cname,
+               (unsigned long)_bd_px_total[cc],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_px_opaque[cc],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_px_skipped[cc],
+               opct_x10);
+      LOG_INFO("[blit-decomp-runs n={} caller={} run_count={} hist_1_3={} hist_4_8={} hist_9_15={} hist_16={}]",
+               n_bd, cname,
+               (unsigned long)_bd_run_count[cc],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_run_hist[cc][0],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_run_hist[cc][1],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_run_hist[cc][2],
+               (unsigned long)_bd_run_hist[cc][3]);
+    }
+  }
+  // patch 0146: reset blit-decomp sample idx + census counters
+  // unconditionally (sample arrays + accumulators overwritten next
+  // block; per-flip accumulators are reset per-flip in flip()).
+  _bd_sample_idx = 0;
+  for (int cc = 0; cc < 2; ++cc)
+  {
+    _bd_px_total[cc]   = 0;
+    _bd_px_opaque[cc]  = 0;
+    _bd_px_skipped[cc] = 0;
+    _bd_run_count[cc]  = 0;
+    _bd_run_hist[cc][0] = 0;
+    _bd_run_hist[cc][1] = 0;
+    _bd_run_hist[cc][2] = 0;
+    _bd_run_hist[cc][3] = 0;
+  }
+
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0124): reset W28 sub-bucket sample idx unconditionally
   // (sample-array contents are overwritten next flip; idx reset lets the
   // cadence repeat cleanly).
@@ -3268,6 +3367,22 @@ bool Renderer::initVideo()
              "(default; set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ASM_BLIT=1 to opt in -- "
              "wave-51 _blit_indexed colorkey-blit lever)");
   }
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0146, Phase 11 wave-51): blit-decomp instrumentation
+  // engagement banner -- greppable witness for build-qa's BANNERS array.
+  if (_blit_decomp_enabled())
+  {
+    LOG_INFO("Renderer::initVideo: blit-decomp _blit_indexed sub-decomp "
+             "instrumentation ENABLED via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP=1 "
+             "-- per-100-flip [blit-decomp-stat] / [blit-decomp-census] / "
+             "[blit-decomp-runs] emitted (wave-51 0145 lever sizing "
+             "ride-along; ~0.1-0.25 ms/flip cost; INSTR cells only)");
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    LOG_INFO("Renderer::initVideo: blit-decomp instrumentation DISABLED "
+             "(default; set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP=1 to opt in -- "
+             "wave-51 _blit_indexed sub-decomp sizing)");
+  }
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0064, Phase 9 wave 13.3): log whether the SDL-side
   // PumpEvents yield-skip is active. Default ON (skip); env-var override
   // SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FORCE_PUMP_YIELD=1 restores the original yield.
@@ -4830,6 +4945,21 @@ void Renderer::flip()
         = (Uint64)_fb_residual;
     ++_flip_body_sample_idx;
   }
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0146, Phase 11 wave-51): push this flip's blit-
+  // decomp phase accumulators into the per-block sample arrays, then
+  // zero the per-flip accumulators. Gated on BLIT_DECOMP; same 100-flip
+  // cadence as flip-stat / flip-body-stat (_maybe_flush_phase_timing_
+  // audit resets _bd_sample_idx every 100 flips). The per-flip
+  // accumulators reset unconditionally so a mid-run enable starts clean.
+  if (_blit_decomp_enabled()
+      && _bd_sample_idx < _flip_phase_block_size)
+  {
+    _bd_dispatch_samples[_bd_sample_idx]  = _bd_dispatch_ns_this_flip;
+    _bd_innerloop_samples[_bd_sample_idx] = _bd_innerloop_ns_this_flip;
+    ++_bd_sample_idx;
+  }
+  _bd_dispatch_ns_this_flip  = 0;
+  _bd_innerloop_ns_this_flip = 0;
   _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit();
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0062, Phase 9 wave 13.1-D2): audio-mixer / engine-
   // tick split (per-100-flip cadence; reads counters bumped by RAII
@@ -5238,6 +5368,15 @@ static inline bool _blit_indexed(SDL_Surface *dst, SDL_Surface *src,
   // calls -- well under the sec. 6 budget).
   const Uint64 _t0 = NXE::Diag::g_mds_tfg_loop_active ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
 
+  // patch 0146 (Phase 11 wave-51): blit-decomp sub-decomp timers. Gated
+  // on SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_BLIT_DECOMP (cached static-const-bool; OFF =
+  // zero-cost -- the three SDL_GetTicksNS reads below are never taken).
+  // Independent of the wave-25 `_t0` brackets above: separate gate,
+  // separate accumulators, nested strictly inside. bi_dispatch = entry
+  // -> clip-done; bi_innerloop = the asm-or-colorkey blit branch.
+  const bool _bd_on = _blit_decomp_enabled();
+  const Uint64 _bd_t0 = _bd_on ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
+
   int dst_x = dstrect.x;
   int dst_y = dstrect.y;
   int sx = srcrect.x;
@@ -5269,6 +5408,12 @@ static inline bool _blit_indexed(SDL_Surface *dst, SDL_Surface *src,
   const Uint8 *sp = (const Uint8 *)src->pixels + sy * src_pitch + sx;
   Uint8 *dp = (Uint8 *)dst->pixels + dst_y * dst_pitch + dst_x;
 
+  // patch 0146 (wave-51): clip-done boundary -- bi_dispatch ends here,
+  // bi_innerloop covers the blit branch below. Early-out (zero-pixel)
+  // calls returned above before this read and are intentionally not
+  // timed (matches the wave-25 don't-count-early-outs convention).
+  const Uint64 _bd_t1 = _bd_on ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
+
   if (has_colorkey && spans)
   {
     // DOS-PORT (patch 0145, wave-51): opaque-span fast path. The
@@ -5308,6 +5453,43 @@ static inline bool _blit_indexed(SDL_Surface *dst, SDL_Surface *src,
       dp += dst_pitch;
     }
   }
+  else if (has_colorkey && _bd_on)
+  {
+    // patch 0146 (wave-51): instrumented colorkey loop -- the legacy
+    // per-pixel path PLUS the px + run census. Lever-INDEPENDENT by
+    // construction: this branch is the colorkey loop, NOT 0145's span
+    // path; with ASM_BLIT=1 (PLAY1) the `has_colorkey && spans` branch
+    // above is taken and this census reads ~0. PLAY2 (ASM_BLIT=0)
+    // yields the baseline px/run census -- that is the 0145 sizing
+    // input. Split by the wave-25 g_mds_tfg_loop_active caller flag:
+    // cc=0 BG/FG tilemap loop, cc=1 sprite/HUD.
+    const int cc = NXE::Diag::g_mds_tfg_loop_active ? 0 : 1;
+    for (int row = 0; row < rows; ++row)
+    {
+      bool in_run = false;
+      int run_len = 0;
+      for (int col = 0; col < cols; ++col)
+      {
+        const Uint8 px = sp[col];
+        if (px != colorkey)
+        {
+          dp[col] = px;
+          ++_bd_px_opaque[cc];
+          if (in_run) { ++run_len; }
+          else { in_run = true; run_len = 1; }
+        }
+        else
+        {
+          ++_bd_px_skipped[cc];
+          if (in_run) { _bd_record_run(cc, run_len); in_run = false; }
+        }
+      }
+      if (in_run) _bd_record_run(cc, run_len);
+      sp += src_pitch;
+      dp += dst_pitch;
+    }
+    _bd_px_total[cc] += (Uint64)rows * (Uint64)cols;
+  }
   else if (has_colorkey)
   {
     for (int row = 0; row < rows; ++row)
@@ -5331,6 +5513,15 @@ static inline bool _blit_indexed(SDL_Surface *dst, SDL_Surface *src,
       dp += dst_pitch;
     }
   }
+  // patch 0146 (wave-51): close the blit-decomp phase timers. Per-flip
+  // accumulation; flip() pushes the per-flip totals into the sample
+  // arrays at the 100-flip emit boundary.
+  if (_bd_on)
+  {
+    const Uint64 _bd_t2 = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+    _bd_dispatch_ns_this_flip += _bd_t1 - _bd_t0;
+    _bd_innerloop_ns_this_flip += _bd_t2 - _bd_t1;
+  }
   if (NXE::Diag::g_mds_tfg_loop_active)
   {
     NXE::Diag::g_mds_tfg_blit_indexed_total_ns += SDL_GetTicksNS() - _t0;
-- 
